.venv/
__pycache__
.aip_traces/
.pytest_cache/

# Lab 7 DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to the defaults above.
#
# .github/ is ordinarily ignored, but the CI regression gate lives there:
# .github/workflows/eval.yml IS the pipeline. Untracked, the gate never runs at
# all, so those negations are load-bearing. `.env` stays ignored.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE. In git the LAST matching pattern wins, so a
# negation written above the rule it overrides does nothing at all. These
# negations used to sit at the top of the file, above the `.aip_cache` rules at
# the bottom -- and `git ls-files .github` came back empty because of it. Keep
# every `!` below the rule it negates.
!
# Note what is NOT here any more: `!.aip_cache/`. It was a no-op, and a
# misleading one -- it read like the cache was about to be committed when it
# never was. See the bottom of this file for why nothing under .aip_cache/ is
# tracked any more, and where the committed cache lives instead.
!.github/
!.github/workflows/
!.github/workflows/eval.yml

Test_by_self
.env
corpus_scaled
ans
zip/*

# THE RESPONSE CACHE. Two files, two jobs, and only one of them is in git.
#
#   .aip_cache/calls.sqlite3    scratch. Every call writes here. 144 MB after an
#                               online warm, because it keeps every corpus
#                               embedding. Never tracked: GitHub rejects any
#                               blob over 100 MB, and trying to commit it is
#                               what broke an earlier push.
#   data/replay/calls.sqlite3   THE REPLAY SET. ~1.3 MB, holding only the keys
#                               offline replay reads (the 45 golden answers,
#                               the Lab 4 judge calls, and the 45 query
#                               vectors). COMMITTED. Rebuilt by
#                               scripts/prune_cache.py.
#
# They are on separate paths so that the 144 MB file cannot be staged by
# accident: the committed one is not under .aip_cache/, so no ignore rule here
# can reach it and no ordering of negations can quietly untrack it. That is the
# whole reason they are not one file -- a single path that was both the
# gitignored scratch and the committed replay set meant any online warm turned
# the tracked file into 144 MB.
#
# tests/test_cache_tracked.py fails the build if the replay set stops being
# tracked or grows past a few MB, because this has now regressed twice.
.aip_cache/

# Machine-specific wall clock from the gate. Deliberately untracked: replaying
# the golden set measures this machine's Python, not the system, and it moves
# every run. reports/gate_metrics.json keeps the reproducible metrics only.
reports/gate_timing.local.json

# Mid-prune scratch file from scripts/prune_cache.py, in case a run is
# interrupted between the VACUUM and the os.replace.
data/replay/*.pruning
